>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Use the aromatic dianionic ligand in the upstream SMILES. Each C₄B₂ ring contains two B atoms with formal charge −1, Each ring has six π electrons. The formal charge on Mo is +4, Both terminal CO ligands are neutral. The molecule has total charge 0. The SDF encodes the aromatic rings with equivalent integer bond orders.

