>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. The deposition distinguishes metal-bound and carbon-bound chlorine. C11 and C14 each carry −1, P3 is +1, Cl1 is −1, Ni(II) balances the net charge to zero. This supports the phosphonium ylide form and distinct assignments for the two chlorines. Localized 24 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The original paper or deposition identifies the ligands, Checked against the supplied coordinates site by site. The atom order and coordinates of all 65 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 66 nonmetal covalent bonds: 65 within range, 1 outside range and 0 with sparse controls. Examples outside range: 6–12 C-F 1.4262 Å. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

