>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Manually reviewed Lewis representation. The original paper reports C₂₇H₂₁Cl₃N₈O₂S₂Zn for compound 3, Removing the CHCl₃ solvent gives C₂₆H₂₀N₈O₂S₂Zn, This matches the input. The authors assign Zn(II) and two monoanionic NNS ligands. The two ligands are equivalent; N=N–C•–S⁻ localizes one electron on each ligand. The radical can delocalize from C• onto sulfur or the hydrazine group. Both N–N distances are 1.304 Å, Both adjacent N–C distances are 1.369 Å. Electron counting guides the choice of radical site, This assignment does not establish the total spin. Localized 24 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. The atom order and coordinates of all 59 atoms agree between XYZ and SDF. Lengths of 60 nonmetal covalent bonds: 60 within range, 0 outside range and 0 with sparse controls. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

